From b8fb472e681863fb42fe2343abda09bd11192015 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccr <ccr@aciceri.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:36:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] collab: mirror the live transcript and phase to the
 owning guest

A remote guest heard the call but saw none of it: the speech recognition of
its own microphone and of the agent reply stayed on the host visualizer.

Forward both through the live bridge as live-transcript and live-phase
frames, targeted at the owner. The guest coalesces updates by role-local
turn, so a streaming turn rewrites its line instead of appending.

LivePanel renders them above the composer as its own surface rather than
inside the session transcript: these lines are volatile recognition, they
rewrite while a turn streams, and they are never persisted. Partial text
is dimmed and italic until the frame is final.

(cherry picked from commit c7ef9b6ef67e2d4b18fae9183d1f94a172bd552a)
